  Product key:  CU-CFHDEFER-040
  Release:      May 21, 2026 (v1.4)

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Purpose:
    Server-side rewrite of Shopify's content_for_header output. Three
    independent rewrite passes:

    Pass 1 (CSS, since v1.0): Flips configured third-party CSS <link>
    tags from media="all" (render-blocking) to media="print"
    onload="this.media='all'" (non-blocking preload-then-apply). Works
    because the media attribute is rewritten before the HTML tokenizer
    sees the tag — Chrome commits the resource as non-render-blocking
    from the start, unlike post-parse rel-swap which commits as
    render-blocking and is too late to uncommit.

    Pass 2 (Klaviyo scripts, since v1.2): Neutralizes Klaviyo bootstrap
    <script src> by changing type to "text/x-cu-deferred". Restorer
    fires on scroll/touchstart.

    Pass 3 (Judge.me CSS comprehensive, NEW v1.3): Segment-split rewrite
    that catches ALL Judge.me CSS link tags regardless of file basename
    or version number. v1.2's Pass 1 only targeted carousels.css for a
    specific Judge.me version (485), and the deployed version had
    bumped to 487, silently breaking the deferral. Pass 3 uses the
    extension UUID as a stable anchor and processes every Judge.me link
    tag's media attribute via segment split + per-segment replace.

  Mechanism:
    Layout captures content_for_header into a local variable and passes
    it to this snippet via the raw_cfh parameter. The snippet runs
    string-replace passes per configured pattern, then emits the
    rewritten output via a single {% raw %}{{ }}{% endraw %} tag.

    Pass 1 CSS: substring match against URL + 2 attribute orderings.
    Pass 2 scripts: split-and-rejoin against bootstrap URL prefix.
    Pass 3 Judge.me: split on extension-UUID + judgeme- marker, then
                     per-segment rewrite of media="all".

  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  v1.3 CHANGELOG (May 1, 2026):
    Pass 3 added: comprehensive Judge.me CSS deferral via segment-split
    technique. Trace investigation May 1 2026 (Slow 4G mobile capture)
    showed:
      - Pass 1's pattern 'judgeme-485/assets/carousels.css' was matching
        ZERO occurrences in CFH because Judge.me had updated to 487.
        carousels.css was loading render-blocking again, exact regression
        the original Pass 1 was meant to prevent.
      - Beyond carousels.css, the Judge.me extension was injecting 14+
        additional CSS files in CFH (Box, Icon, Text, Center, layout,
        JLightbox, JmModal, ReviewItem, Cluster, StarRating, ReviewContent,
        Frame, Button, widget_v3_base, JLightboxCarousel, JLightboxContent),
        all loading render-blocking with hash-suffixed basenames that
        rotate on Judge.me updates.

    Pass 3 strategy:
      Stable anchor = extension UUID (019e5099-1de6-7336-964a-9101e667bb29)
      + literal '/judgeme-' (catches any version: 485, 486, 487, ...).
      Split CFH on this anchor. Each segment after the first contains
      exactly one Judge.me URL tail + the closing tag attributes.
      In each such segment, replace the FIRST occurrence of
      ' media="all">' (and its 2 attribute-ordering variants) with the
      print-then-onload swap. The replace is FIRST-occurrence-only
      (via split+join with limit) so unrelated media="all" tags later
      in the segment are untouched.

    Pattern resilience:
      - Judge.me version bumps (487 → 488 → ...) — UNAFFECTED, anchor
        catches all versions
      - Judge.me hash rotations on individual files — UNAFFECTED, no
        per-file matching
      - Judge.me changing extension UUID — would break, but extension
        UUIDs are stable for the lifetime of an extension installation.
        If Judge.me is uninstalled and reinstalled, update the anchor
        constant below
      - Pass 1's old judgeme-485/carousels.css pattern: now redundant
        but kept as safety net (no harm if it fails to match)

    Predicted impact: removes ~12-15 render-blocking CSS link tags from
    initial paint, frees ~150KB of bandwidth contention in the 664-666ms
    window. Estimated LCP improvement on Slow 4G: 500-1500ms.

  v1.2 CHANGELOG (April 28, 2026):
    Added Pass 2: server-side neutralization of Klaviyo bootstrap. See
    full notes preserved below for context.

  v1.1 CHANGELOG (April 24, 2026):
    Documentation hygiene pass.

  v1.0 INITIAL RELEASE:
    Pure Liquid server-side rewrite of content_for_header. Initial
    pattern: judgeme-485/assets/carousels.css.
